on"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288143"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-288593"] :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=q-1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq-1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-1 & =0 \\\\ q & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-288646/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "390874bc-bfd8-578c-90b5-a69ca89dfaed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288646/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c50eb8a-ba2d-559e-9d3b-3ecc0ed9a818" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288646/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-288646/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288646" :question/id #uuid "d6f2f316-a4ef-51a7-99f1-5d44fefeac54" :question/math-academy-id "q-288646" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n(m+6)x+2=7\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $m?$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+6)x+2 & =7 \\\\ (m+6)x+2-2 & =7-2 \\\\ {{(m+6)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{5}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nm+6=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+6 & =0 \\\\ m & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288646/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288646"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288648/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "ae7582f2-02b5-5d13-969e-f059e51cfb49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288648/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "655c1563-4247-5421-aad0-8de8729e158f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288648/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecde7c59-4b71-5d7f-9e56-2edb8d2fa1cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288648/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-288648/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-288648/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288648" :question/id #uuid "e5aeefd8-dd0b-554b-bac9-09059b0855e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-288648" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $u,$ given by\n\n$$\n(q-5)u+9=0\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(q-5)u+9 & =0 \\\\ (q-5)u+9-9 & =0-9 \\\\ {{(q-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}u & ={{-9}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-5 & =0 \\\\ q & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288648/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288648"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288634/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "24d10d47-f933-561e-af9e-138002f6c5b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288634/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "db24cc88-516f-5f07-8fef-8e2dc0303186" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288634/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-288634/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288634" :question/id #uuid "4bf47b67-ad18-5292-b32f-954004aeb3fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-288634" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n3(p+2)x+7=10\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(p+2)x+7 & =10 \\\\ 3(p+2)x+7-7 & =10-7 \\\\ {{3(p+2)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3(p+2)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(p+2) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3(p+2)}{3} & =\\frac{0}{3} \\\\ p+2 & =0 \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288634/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288634"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288644/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1e26f11a-958e-573c-8fc9-e3595a06e50f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288644/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "39d860c2-c6b2-5646-821c-92bb62d8c2a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288644/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "76181339-5cd7-5650-b143-bb2c8db6135d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288644/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-288644/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-288644/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288644" :question/id #uuid "9021d130-3d7b-513a-93e6-cae05d8662af" :question/math-academy-id "q-288644" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n(k-2)v-3=5\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(k-2)v-3 & =5 \\\\ (k-2)v-3+3 & =5+3 \\\\ {{(k-2)}_{⏟}}_{a}v & ={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nk-2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-2 & =0 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288644/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-287667"] :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4)x+2 & =5 \\\\ 2(p-4)x+2-2 & =5-2 \\\\ {{2(p-4)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(p-4)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(p-4)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ p-4 & =0 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-288678/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "bca33de8-9206-5066-b587-df197193ba48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288678/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "68a9b56b-9708-530f-8a62-21763e71626a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288678/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-288678/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288678" :question/id #uuid "53621c2d-b714-55a4-bb17-dd8e78db13a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288678" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-3pz-8=-z-6\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $z$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz-8 & =-z-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-z-6+z \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz+z-8 & =-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8+8 & =-6+8 \\\\ -3pz+z & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-3p+1)z=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-3p+1)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{2}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-3p+1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3p+1 & =0 \\\\ -3p+1-1 & =0-1 \\\\ -3p & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{-3p}{-3} & =\\frac{-1}{-3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288678/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288678"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288675/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "8c5cc0a8-f03b-552a-8e72-3f8d5b2498be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288675/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a047952d-53ad-53c0-93f8-e21be9834333" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288675/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "201e427b-6e02-5156-8cfe-a29c280f0e79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288675/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-288675/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-288675/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288675" :question/id #uuid "877e1227-8365-5e43-86f2-3ed7e56a5b5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-288675" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $w,$ given by\n\n$$\n-4mw+5=-3w+1\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $m?$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $aw=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $3w$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4mw+5 & =-3w+1 \\\\ -4mw+3w+5 & =-3w+1+3w \\\\ -4mw+3w+5 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4mw+3w+5 & =1 \\\\ -4mw+3w+5-5 & =1-5 \\\\ -4mw+3w & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $w$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-4m+3)w=-4.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $aw=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-4m+3)}_{⏟}}_{a}w={{-4}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-4m+3=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4m+3 & =0 \\\\ -4m+3-3 & =0-3 \\\\ -4m & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{-4m}{-4} & =\\frac{-3}{-4} \\\\ m & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288675/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288675"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288674/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "dab68e7c-7769-5198-8881-83b60f206c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288674/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc06a7c-b201-563d-838b-13bc201fd4f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288674/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer-field/choices ["q-288674/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288674" :question/id #uuid "f2f67ac6-2a69-5d98-9eb7-bfa977c1a594" :question/math-academy-id "q-288674" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $u,$ given by\n\n$$\n5ru+3=2u+6\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $au=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $2u$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ru+3 & =2u+6 \\\\ 5ru-2u+3 & =2u+6-2u \\\\ 5ru-2u+3 & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ru-2u+3 & =6 \\\\ 5ru-2u+3-3 & =6-3 \\\\ 5ru-2u & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $u$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(5r-2)u=3.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(5r-2)}_{⏟}}_{a}u={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5r-2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5r-2 & =0 \\\\ 5r-2+2 & =0+2 \\\\ 5r & =2 \\\\ \\frac{5r}{5} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ r & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288674/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288673/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "dce29a62-1b39-597a-a127-fc69af7bfb2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288673/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "94f07611-43e2-5403-ae2e-311a95f08b08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288673/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0b495d4-9421-58a5-a258-9fce37cad603" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288673/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer-field/choices ["q-288673/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-288673/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288673" :question/id #uuid "29b2eed1-2fce-5eb7-8c1b-247497813df5" :question/math-academy-id "q-288673" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n3qz+4=7z+1\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $7z$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3qz+4 & =7z+1 \\\\ 3qz-7z+4 & =7z+1-7z \\\\ 3qz-7z+4 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $4$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3qz-7z+4 & =1 \\\\ 3qz-7z+4-4 & =1-4 \\\\ 3qz-7z & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3q-7)z=-3.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3q-7)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{-3}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3q-7=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3q-7 & =0 \\\\ 3q-7+7 & =0+7 \\\\ 3q & =7 \\\\ \\frac{3q}{3} & =\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ q & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288673/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288673"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288662/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "c8b1b9c0-a2e5-54d6-8ca2-b1cc23935b23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288662/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "3df5b0de-5ab5-57e4-949b-8a019f9a7fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288662/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "e8a86eb1-d43c-52b0-8a83-3f4b2861b4f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288662/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "45166757-4947-5d25-afe0-cb04e8d26352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288662/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "4a668c7e-53b0-5fdc-9fd6-7a96bf353f7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288662/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e70af324-e6b8-5133-9ebf-4d27f28209f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-288662/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer-field/choices ["q-288662/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-288662/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-288662/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-288662/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-288662/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288662" :question/id #uuid "65b5657a-e041-5dba-9476-47eab2ebbed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288662" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n3py=5y+8\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ay=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $5y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3py & =5y+8 \\\\ 3py-5y & =5y+8-5y \\\\ 3py-5y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $y$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3p-5)y=8.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ay=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3p-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}y={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3p-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-5 & =0 \\\\ 3p-5+5 & =0+5 \\\\ 3p & =5 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{3} & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288662/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67"] :knowledge-point/questions ["